Here is your formal test smell audit of `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` using the **testsmells.org 19-smell academic catalog**.

---

## Calibration Note

The class is annotated `[TestCategory("Integration")]`, so **integration-test calibration** applies: Mystery Guest and Eager Test severity are downgraded for patterns appropriate at integration scope (e.g., using a real SQLite connection is expected). Smells that cause false-passes or non-determinism remain at full severity even for integration tests.

---

## Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 3           | 3              |
| Medium   | 1           | 1              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

## Findings by Severity

### 🔴 HIGH 1 — Sleepy Test

**Smell:** Sleepy Test  
**Method:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 87)  
**Risk:** Non-deterministic — 3 s may be too short on slow CI, too long for fast runs. Adds 3 s to every suite execution.

```csharp
// ❌ Current
Thread.Sleep(3000);
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Fix — poll with a timeout instead of a fixed sleep:**

```csharp
// ✅ Remediated
var cts = new CancellationTokenSource(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));
while (!_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
{
    await Task.Delay(100, cts.Token);   // fast poll, bounded timeout
}
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

---

### 🔴 HIGH 2 — Conditional Test Logic

**Smell:** Conditional Test Logic  
**Method:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (lines 101–108)  
**Risk:** One branch is never exercised because `Insert` always creates a plain `User`, not a `PremiumUser`. The `if` arm is dead code, giving false coverage confidence.

```csharp
// ❌ Current
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Fix — split into two deterministic tests:**

```csharp
// ✅ Remediated — test 1: standard user path
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    var user = new User("eve@example.com", "Eve");
    _repository.Insert(user);
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");
    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

// ✅ Remediated — test 2: premium user path (needs premium seed data)
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    var user = new PremiumUser("vip@example.com", "VIP", discountRate: 0.15m);
    _repository.Insert(user);
    var loaded = (PremiumUser)_repository.GetByEmail("vip@example.com")!;
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

---

### 🔴 HIGH 3 — Assertion-Free Test (a.k.a. Unknown Test)

**Smell:** Assertion-Free Test  
**Method:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (lines 113–119)  
**Risk:** This test will pass even if every insert silently corrupts data. It only proves no exception is thrown — a very weak guarantee.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — no assertion at all
for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
{
    _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
}
```

**Fix — assert that the bulk data was actually persisted:**

```csharp
// ✅ Remediated
for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
{
    _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
}
var all = _repository.ListAll();
Assert.AreEqual(100, all.Count);
CollectionAssert.AllItemsAreUnique(
    all.Select(u => u.Email).ToList());
```

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM 1 — Assertion Roulette

**Smell:** Assertion Roulette *(extended catalog)*  
**Method:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (lines 35–38)  
**Risk:** Four assertions with no message parameters. When one fails in CI, the stack trace shows `Assert.AreEqual failed` with no context about *which* property was wrong.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — 4 bare assertions
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Fix — add discriminating messages:**

```csharp
// ✅ Remediated
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Id should be assigned by the database");
```

---

## Smell-Free Patterns 👍

The remaining **4 tests** are well-designed:

| Test | What's good |
|------|-------------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange-act-assert, focused on one behavior |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Verifies absence correctly with `Assert.IsNull` |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count assertion is self-documenting (3 inserts → expect 3) |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Good concurrency stress test with clear assertion |

The **General Fixture** (Smell 9) does **not** apply — both `_connection` and `_repository` are used by every test. Setup is appropriately scoped.

---

## Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Effort |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| 1 | **Assertion-Free Test** (`BulkInsert…`) | Add count + uniqueness assertions | ~2 min |
| 2 | **Conditional Test Logic** (`GetUser…`) | Split into two deterministic tests | ~5 min |
| 3 | **Sleepy Test** (`NotifyOnInsert…`) | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with polling loop + timeout | ~5 min |
| 4 | **Assertion Roulette** (`InsertUser…`) | Add message strings to the 4 assertions | ~2 min |

Fix priorities 1–3 first — they can cause **false passes** or **flaky failures**. Priority 4 is a maintainability improvement that pays off at scale.
